{
  "slug": "cayleys-theorem-oq-01-oq-02-oq-02",
  "title": "The Outer Automorphism Exact Sequence 1 → Inn(G) → Aut(G) → Out(G) → 1",
  "phase": "OBSERVE",
  "status": "available",
  "tier": "B",
  "path": "full",
  "problemStatement": {
    "formal": "1 \\longrightarrow \\operatorname{Inn}(G) \\xrightarrow{\\iota} \\operatorname{Aut}(G) \\xrightarrow{\\pi} \\operatorname{Out}(G) \\longrightarrow 1, \\text{ where } \\operatorname{Inn}(G) = (\\operatorname{MulAut.conj})\\text{.range} \\trianglelefteq \\operatorname{Aut}(G),\\ \\operatorname{Out}(G) := \\operatorname{Aut}(G) / \\operatorname{Inn}(G),\\ \\ker \\pi = \\operatorname{im}\\iota = \\operatorname{Inn}(G), \\text{ and } G / Z(G) \\cong \\operatorname{Inn}(G).",
    "plain": "Every group G has an automorphism group Aut(G). The inner automorphisms are the maps conj_g : x ↦ g·x·g⁻¹; the parent entry showed g ↦ conj_g has kernel Z(G), so Inn(G) ≅ G/Z(G). This follow-up formalizes that Inn(G) is a normal subgroup of Aut(G), so the quotient Out(G) = Aut(G)/Inn(G) is a group, and assembles the short exact sequence 1 → Inn(G) → Aut(G) → Out(G) → 1.",
    "whyMatters": [
      "Out(G) is a fundamental invariant measuring symmetries of G not realized by conjugation; it governs group extensions and the theory of complete groups (Z(G)=1 and Out(G)=1 give Aut(G) ≅ G).",
      "The sequence promotes the parent's G/Z(G) ≅ Inn(G) from an isolated isomorphism into the first term of the canonical exact sequence organizing the automorphism tower.",
      "Computations of Out(G) for simple groups (e.g. the exceptional Out(S₆)) are classification-level data that all rest on this exact sequence."
    ]
  },
  "knownResults": {
    "proven": [],
    "open": [
      "Define Inn(G) as (MulAut.conj (G := G)).range : Subgroup (MulAut G) as a first-class object.",
      "Prove Inn(G) is normal in Aut(G) via the identity φ ∘ conj_g ∘ φ⁻¹ = conj_(φ g).",
      "Define Out(G) := MulAut G ⧸ (MulAut.conj).range and prove exactness: ker π = Inn(G), π surjective, ι injective."
    ],
    "goal": "Define Inn(G) = (MulAut.conj).range, prove Subgroup.Normal, define Out G := MulAut G ⧸ Inn G, and assemble the short exact sequence 1 → Inn(G) → Aut(G) → Out(G) → 1 with exactness at each term, reusing the parent's G/Z(G) ≅ Inn(G) to describe the first term."
  },
